---
permalink: /404.html
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
notFound: true
ownOpening: true
title: "Page not found | Lightening Lives"
description: "This page is not here. The address may be from our old website, or the page may have moved."
social: /assets/img/social.png
closing: false
---
{#- Not found (content file 5.18; old addresses 3.4), redone 25 October 2026 (the user: "funny or
    funky"). The page reads as a test result in the company's own language: a gel where the expected
    lane shows its band at 404 and the visitor's address shows none, stamped NOT DETECTED. With script
    the bands run down the gel on arrival, the visitor's address is printed as the sample, and "Run it
    again" re-runs the gel (the result never changes, the line under it does). Without script, or with
    reduced motion, the gel is still. GitHub Pages serves this file at any address it has no page for,
    so every link and asset is root-relative. For an old .php address not-found.js adds one line above
    the links naming the new page (Review Focus 4). No closing band; no canonical or card of its own. -#}
{%- set arrow = '<svg aria-hidden="true" width="26" height="16" viewBox="0 0 26 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2"><path d="M1 8h22M16 1l7 7-7 7"/></svg>' %}
{%- set links = [
  { text: "Home", href: "/" },
  { text: "Solutions", href: "/solutions/" },
  { text: "Partners", href: "/partners/" },
  { text: "Our work", href: "/our-work/" },
  { text: "About", href: "/about/" },
  { text: "Contact", href: "/contact/" }
] %}

  <section class="section page-open lost" aria-labelledby="page-h" data-not-found>
    <div class="wrap lost-grid">
      <div class="lost-head">
        <h1 id="page-h" class="display">We ran the test. <span class="h-mark">No page detected.</span></h1>
        <p class="lead lost-lead">The address may be from our old website, or the page may have moved.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="lost-ways">
        <p class="lost-to">These lead to the same things:</p>
        <ul class="actions">
          {%- for link in links %}
          <li><a class="action" href="{{ link.href }}">{{ link.text }}{{ arrow | safe }}</a></li>
          {%- endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>

      <figure class="lost-gel" data-lost-gel>
        <div class="gel-slab lost-slab" role="img" aria-label="A gel, for fun: the expected lane shows a band at 404; the lane for your address shows no band, stamped not detected.">
          {%- set ladder = [14, 22, 30, 38, 46, 54, 62, 70, 78, 86] %}
          <div class="lane lane-marker">
            <span class="lane-name">Marker</span>
            <div class="lane-track"><span class="lane-well"></span>{% for y in ladder %}<span class="lane-band{% if y == 46 %} is-heavy{% endif %}" style="--y: {{ y }}%"></span>{% endfor %}</div>
          </div>
          <div class="lane lane-expected">
            <span class="lane-name">Expected</span>
            <div class="lane-track"><span class="lane-well"></span><span class="lane-band" style="--y: 46%"></span><span class="lost-size" style="--y: 46%">404</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="lane lane-yours">
            <span class="lane-name">Your address</span>
            <div class="lane-track"><span class="lane-well"></span><span class="lost-ghost" style="--y: 46%"></span></div>
          </div>
          <span class="lost-stamp" aria-hidden="true">Not detected</span>
        </div>
        <figcaption class="lost-slip">
          <span class="lost-sample" data-lost-sample hidden>Sample: <code></code></span>
          <span class="lost-line" data-lost-line aria-live="polite">Result: no band where the page should be.</span>
          <button type="button" class="lost-rerun" data-lost-rerun hidden>{% icon "rotate-ccw" %}Run it again</button>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>
